# EtBottomSheet v2 Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtBottomSheet` is a wrapper around `@gorhom/bottom-sheet` (v5+) that provides a compound component API for modal bottom sheets in the eToro design system.

### Features

- **Compound component pattern**: `EtBottomSheet.Header`, `EtBottomSheet.Content`, `EtBottomSheet.Footer`
- **Floating drag handle**: Handle indicator floats above the sheet background
- **Header compound API**: `Header.Title` and `Header.Action` for flexible header composition
- **Dynamic sizing**: Automatically sizes to content height
- **Scrollable content**: Uses `BottomSheetScrollView` when `scrollable={true}`
- **Virtualized lists**: `List`, `SectionList`, and `FlashList` for large datasets
- **Sticky footer**: Keyboard-aware footer using `BottomSheetFooter`
- **Loading state**: Built-in loading indicator with custom placeholder support
- **Accessibility**: Screen reader announcements, reduced motion support
- **Animation presets**: `smooth`, `bouncy` (default), `fast` open/close spring styles

### Does NOT Handle

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Custom `WithSpringConfig` overrides (use `animationPreset` presets instead)
- Initial open state via `index` prop (use imperative API instead)

### Opening and Closing the Sheet

The sheet is controlled imperatively via the `bottomSheetRef`:

```tsx
const sheetRef = useRef<BottomSheetModal | null>(null);

// Open the sheet
sheetRef.current?.present();

// Close the sheet
sheetRef.current?.dismiss();

// Snap to specific index
sheetRef.current?.snapToIndex(1);
```

**Note:** The library's `index` prop for initial state is not exposed. This is intentional - `BottomSheetModal` is designed to start closed and be presented imperatively. Use `present()` in a `useEffect` if you need the sheet open on mount.

## IMPORTANT: BottomSheetModalProvider Requirement

**The `EtBottomSheet` component MUST be used within a `BottomSheetModalProvider`** from `@gorhom/bottom-sheet`.

```tsx
import { BottomSheetModalProvider } from '@gorhom/bottom-sheet';
import { GestureHandlerRootView } from 'react-native-gesture-handler';

// At app root:
<GestureHandlerRootView style={{ flex: 1 }}>
  <BottomSheetModalProvider>
    <YourApp />
  </BottomSheetModalProvider>
</GestureHandlerRootView>;
```

## Header Patterns

### Compound Header (recommended for most cases)

Use `Header.Title` and `Header.Action` subcomponents for title + actions.

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Settings</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header.Action onPress={handleClose} accessibilityLabel="Close">
    <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'close' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
  </EtBottomSheet.Header.Action>
</EtBottomSheet.Header>
```

**Title** renders centered `heading-compact` text. Accepts all `EtTextProps` for overrides.
**Action** is a `Pressable` with `accessibilityRole="button"` and `hitSlop=10`. Always positioned at the trailing edge.

### Title Only

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Select Option</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
</EtBottomSheet.Header>
```

### Close Button Only (no title)

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header.Action onPress={handleClose} accessibilityLabel="Close">
    <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'close' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
  </EtBottomSheet.Header.Action>
</EtBottomSheet.Header>
```

### Custom Content Header

For fully custom header content (e.g., search input), pass arbitrary children. The Header falls back to default padding without compound layout.

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <BottomSheetTextInput placeholder="Search..." value={searchText} onChangeText={setSearchText} />
</EtBottomSheet.Header>
```

### Mixed Custom + Action

You can mix custom content with `Header.Action` — Action children are separated to the trailing edge.

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 8 }}>
    <Image source={{ uri: imageUrl }} style={styles.logo} />
    <EtText variant="label-primary-semibold">{symbolName}</EtText>
  </View>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header.Action onPress={handleClose} accessibilityLabel="Close">
    <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'close' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
  </EtBottomSheet.Header.Action>
</EtBottomSheet.Header>
```

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtBottomSheet` (main component)

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet
  // Required
  bottomSheetRef={RefObject<BottomSheetModal>}

  // Sizing
  snapPoints?: (number | string)[]              // disables dynamic sizing
  enableDynamicSizing?: boolean                 // default: true
  maxDynamicContentSize?: number                // auto-calculated for scrollable
  topInset?: number                             // top safe area inset
  bottomInset?: number                          // bottom safe area inset

  // Behavior
  onOpen?: () => void                           // called when sheet opens
  onClose?: () => void                          // called when sheet closes (animation complete)
  onBeforeClose?: () => boolean | void          // called before close, return false to prevent
  onChange?: (index: number) => void            // sheet snap point changed
  onAnimate?: (fromIndex, toIndex, fromPosition, toPosition) => void  // animation start with positions
  closeOnBackdrop?: boolean                     // default: true
  enablePanDownToClose?: boolean                // default: true (note: library default is false)
  animationPreset?: 'smooth' | 'bouncy' | 'fast' // default: 'bouncy' — open/close spring style
  enableContentPanningGesture?: boolean         // default: true
  enableHandlePanningGesture?: boolean          // default: true
  enableOverDrag?: boolean                      // default: true
  overDragResistanceFactor?: number             // default: 2.5
  detached?: boolean                            // default: false (floating modal)

  // Animation (Advanced)
  animatedIndex?: SharedValue<number>           // for external animation coordination
  animatedPosition?: SharedValue<number>        // for position-based effects (parallax)

  // Keyboard
  keyboardBehavior?: 'extend' | 'fillParent' | 'interactive'  // default: 'interactive'
  keyboardBlurBehavior?: 'none' | 'restore'     // default: 'none'
  enableBlurKeyboardOnGesture?: boolean         // default: false
  android_keyboardInputMode?: 'adjustPan' | 'adjustResize'    // default: 'adjustPan'

  // Appearance
  showHandle?: boolean                          // default: true
  backdrop?: BackdropConfig                     // { enabled?, onPress? } - enabled by default
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>                  // sheet container style
  backgroundStyle?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>        // sheet background style
  loading?: boolean                             // default: false

  // Accessibility
  accessibilityLabel?: string
  testID?: string
>
  {children}
</EtBottomSheet>
```

### Subcomponents

#### `EtBottomSheet.Header`

Compound component with `Title` and `Action` subcomponents.

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Header style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> testID?: string>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Title</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header.Action onPress={fn} accessibilityLabel="Close">
    <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'close' }} />
  </EtBottomSheet.Header.Action>
</EtBottomSheet.Header>
```

**Header.Title** - Extends `EtTextProps`. Defaults: `variant="heading-compact"`, `numberOfLines=1`, `textAlign: 'center'`.
**Header.Action** - Extends `PressableProps`. Defaults: `accessibilityRole="button"`, `hitSlop=10`. Always trailing.

#### `EtBottomSheet.Content`

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Content
  scrollable?: boolean              // default: false
  loadingPlaceholder?: ReactNode    // custom loading UI
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>
>
  {children}
</EtBottomSheet.Content>
```

#### `EtBottomSheet.Footer`

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Footer
  transparent?: boolean              // default: false — drop the solid background layer
  scrollFade?: SharedValue<number>   // gradient above the footer, see below
>
  {/* EtButtonV2 components */}
</EtBottomSheet.Footer>
```

Note: Footer styling is handled by the parent component. Content is rendered with consistent padding and safe area handling — do not re-add `paddingTop` in your footer content.

`scrollFade` dissolves scrolling content into the footer when there is more to scroll. Pass the remaining distance to the bottom (`max(contentHeight - viewportHeight - scrollOffset, 0)`), fed by the sheet's `onScroll`, `onContentSizeChange` and `onScrollViewLayout`. The last two matter: RN never fires `onScroll` from mounting alone, so without them the gradient stays invisible until the first scroll gesture. The footer positions the gradient above its own opaque box — placing it inside the footer paints the surface color over the identical background and shows nothing.

## Usage Patterns

### Basic sheet with title and close

```tsx
const sheetRef = useRef<BottomSheetModal | null>(null);

<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef} onClose={handleClose}>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Select Option</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Action onPress={() => sheetRef.current?.dismiss()} accessibilityLabel="Close">
      <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'close' }} appearance={{ size: 24 }} />
    </EtBottomSheet.Header.Action>
  </EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Content>
    <YourContent />
  </EtBottomSheet.Content>
  <EtBottomSheet.Footer>
    <EtButtonV2 variant="primary-filled" onPress={handleConfirm}>
      Confirm
    </EtButtonV2>
  </EtBottomSheet.Footer>
</EtBottomSheet>;
```

### Search header with custom content

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet
  bottomSheetRef={sheetRef}
  snapPoints={['60%']}
>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>
    <BottomSheetTextInput value={searchText} onChangeText={setSearchText} placeholder="Search..." />
  </EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Content scrollable>
    <SearchResults items={filteredItems} />
  </EtBottomSheet.Content>
</EtBottomSheet>
```

### Confirmation dialog (prevent accidental close)

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef} closeOnBackdrop={false} enablePanDownToClose={false}>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Delete Account?</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
  </EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Content>
    <EtText>This action cannot be undone.</EtText>
  </EtBottomSheet.Content>
  <EtBottomSheet.Footer>
    <EtButtonV2 variant="negative-filled" onPress={handleDelete}>
      Delete
    </EtButtonV2>
    <EtButtonV2 variant="primary-subtle" onPress={handleCancel}>
      Cancel
    </EtButtonV2>
  </EtBottomSheet.Footer>
</EtBottomSheet>
```

### Multiple actions in header

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef}>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Edit Profile</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Action onPress={handleReset} accessibilityLabel="Reset">
      <EtoroIcon icon={{ iconName: 'refresh' }} />
    </EtBottomSheet.Header.Action>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Action onPress={handleSave} accessibilityLabel="Save">
      <EtText style={{ color: colors.primary600 }}>Save</EtText>
    </EtBottomSheet.Header.Action>
  </EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Content>
    <ProfileForm />
  </EtBottomSheet.Content>
</EtBottomSheet>
```

## Anti-patterns

### Using subcomponents outside EtBottomSheet

```tsx
// BAD - context not available
<EtBottomSheet.Content>
  <Text>Content</Text>
</EtBottomSheet.Content>
```

### Multiple of same subcomponent

```tsx
// BAD - throws runtime error
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef}>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>...</EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>...</EtBottomSheet.Header> // Error!
</EtBottomSheet>
```

### Missing BottomSheetModalProvider

```tsx
// BAD - will not render
<App>
  <EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef}>...</EtBottomSheet>
</App>

// GOOD - wrap with provider
<GestureHandlerRootView style={{ flex: 1 }}>
  <BottomSheetModalProvider>
    <App>
      <EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef}>...</EtBottomSheet>
    </App>
  </BottomSheetModalProvider>
</GestureHandlerRootView>
```

### Using regular TextInput

```tsx
// BAD - won't work properly
<EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <TextInput placeholder="Search..." />
</EtBottomSheet.Header>

// GOOD - use BottomSheetTextInput
<EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <BottomSheetTextInput placeholder="Search..." />
</EtBottomSheet.Header>
```

### Using index prop for initial state

```tsx
// BAD - index prop is not exposed; BottomSheetModal starts closed by design
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef} index={0}>
  ...
</EtBottomSheet>;

// GOOD - use imperative API to open on mount
useEffect(() => {
  sheetRef.current?.present();
}, []);
```

### Using regular FlatList/ScrollView inside Content

```tsx
// BAD - gesture conflicts, scrolling won't work properly
<EtBottomSheet.Content scrollable>
  <FlatList data={items} renderItem={...} />
</EtBottomSheet.Content>

// GOOD - use EtBottomSheet.List for virtualized lists
<EtBottomSheet.List
  data={items}
  renderItem={...}
  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}
/>

// GOOD - for horizontal lists, use react-native-gesture-handler
import { FlatList } from 'react-native-gesture-handler';
```

### Stacking sheets (sub-sheets opened from within another sheet)

When you present a second `EtBottomSheet` while another is already open
(e.g. a fee/info sub-sheet opened from a confirmation sheet), gorhom's
default `stackBehavior='switch'` **minimizes the parent sheet**. In
hosting trees where the parent's `onClose` resets the data backing the
sheet (a common controller pattern), the parent's React tree unmounts,
which then unmounts the freshly-presented sub-sheet too — the sub-sheet
appears to "close right away".

Pass `stackBehavior="push"` on the sub-sheet so the parent stays
presented underneath:

```tsx
// BAD - nesting sheets in the JSX tree (parent owns the JSX, but gorhom
// renders modals via a Portal, so the JSX position doesn't control z-index).
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={parentRef}>
  <EtBottomSheet.Content>
    <EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={childRef}>...</EtBottomSheet>
  </EtBottomSheet.Content>
</EtBottomSheet>;

// GOOD - render sub-sheet as a sibling, present imperatively, and use
// stackBehavior="push" so the parent stays mounted/presented behind it.
function ParentSheet({ parentRef }) {
  const childRef = useRef<BottomSheetModal | null>(null);
  return (
    <>
      <EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={parentRef}>...</EtBottomSheet>
      <EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={childRef} stackBehavior="push">
        ...
      </EtBottomSheet>
    </>
  );
}
```

`stackBehavior` accepts:

- `'switch'` (default) — minimize the previous modal; restore on dismiss.
  Suited to sheet-to-sheet **navigation** where the second sheet replaces
  the first in the user's focus.
- `'push'` — stack on top without touching the previous modal. Use for
  **tooltip / info sub-sheets** so the parent stays presented and its
  state is left alone.
- `'replace'` — fully dismiss the previous modal (its `onClose` fires) and
  do not restore it.

### Dismissing without handling keyboard

```tsx
// BAD - keyboard may stay visible after sheet closes
const handleSubmit = () => {
  sheetRef.current?.dismiss();
};

// GOOD - dismiss keyboard before closing sheet
import { Keyboard } from 'react-native';

const handleSubmit = () => {
  Keyboard.dismiss();
  sheetRef.current?.dismiss();
};
```

