## Known Limitations

### TextInput Focus

Regular `TextInput` components don't work properly inside the sheet due to gesture handling conflicts. Always use `BottomSheetTextInput` from `@gorhom/bottom-sheet`.

### Virtualized Lists

For large lists, use virtualized components for optimal performance:

#### `EtBottomSheet.List` (FlatList-based)

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef} snapPoints={['50%', '90%']}>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Select Item</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
  </EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.List
    data={items}
    renderItem={({ item }) => <ItemRow item={item} />}
    keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}
    ItemSeparatorComponent={() => <View style={{ height: 8 }} />}
  />
  <EtBottomSheet.Footer>
    <EtButtonV2 variant="primary-filled" onPress={handleConfirm}>
      Confirm
    </EtButtonV2>
  </EtBottomSheet.Footer>
</EtBottomSheet>
```

#### `EtBottomSheet.SectionList` (Grouped data)

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.SectionList
  sections={[
    { title: 'Favorites', data: favorites },
    { title: 'Recent', data: recent },
  ]}
  renderItem={({ item }) => <ItemRow item={item} />}
  renderSectionHeader={({ section }) => <SectionHeader title={section.title} />}
  keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}
/>
```

#### `EtBottomSheet.FlashList` (Best performance)

For the best performance with very large lists (100+ items), use FlashList which provides cell recycling:

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef} snapPoints={['50%', '90%']}>
  <EtBottomSheet.Header>
    <EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>Select Asset</EtBottomSheet.Header.Title>
  </EtBottomSheet.Header>
  <EtBottomSheet.FlashList
    data={assets}
    renderItem={({ item }) => <AssetRow asset={item} />}
    keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}
  />
</EtBottomSheet>
```

**FlashList Notes:**

- **`keyExtractor` is required** - Enforced at compile-time to prevent visual glitches during upward scrolling
- **Automatic size estimation** - No need to provide `estimatedItemSize`
- **Improved blank cell handling** - Better algorithms for preventing blank cells
- **Simplified API** - `overrideItemLayout` only supports `span` (size is automatic)

**When to use each:**

- **`EtBottomSheet.Content`** - Static content, forms (< 20 items)
- **`EtBottomSheet.Content scrollable`** - Simple scrollable content (20-50 items)
- **`EtBottomSheet.List`** - Standard virtualized lists (50-100 items)
- **`EtBottomSheet.SectionList`** - Grouped/sectioned data (50-100 items)
- **`EtBottomSheet.FlashList`** - Maximum performance (100+ items)

**Note:** When using `EtBottomSheet.List`, `EtBottomSheet.SectionList`, or `EtBottomSheet.FlashList`, always provide `snapPoints`. The component will automatically disable dynamic sizing for virtualized lists and log a warning in development mode if `snapPoints` is not provided.

### Close Callback Timing

The component provides two close-related callbacks with different timing:

- **`onBeforeClose`** - Fires BEFORE dismiss animation starts. Return `false` to prevent close.
- **`onClose`** - Fires AFTER dismiss animation completes.

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet
  onBeforeClose={() => {
    if (hasUnsavedChanges) {
      showConfirmation();
      return false; // Prevent close
    }
  }}
  onClose={() => {
    // Cleanup after sheet is fully closed
    resetForm();
  }}
/>
```

## Troubleshooting

### Pressables/Touchables not working on Android

Due to gesture handler wrapping, standard React Native touchables may not work. Use touchables from `@gorhom/bottom-sheet`:

```tsx
import { TouchableOpacity, TouchableHighlight, TouchableWithoutFeedback } from '@gorhom/bottom-sheet';
```

### Horizontal ScrollView/FlatList not working on Android

Use `ScrollView` and `FlatList` from `react-native-gesture-handler` instead of `react-native`:

```tsx
import { ScrollView, FlatList } from 'react-native-gesture-handler';
```

### TextInput keyboard issues

Always use `BottomSheetTextInput` instead of regular `TextInput`:

```tsx
import { BottomSheetTextInput } from '@gorhom/bottom-sheet';

<BottomSheetTextInput placeholder="Search..." value={text} onChangeText={setText} />;
```

### Content panning gesture conflicts with scrollable content

The component auto-disables `enableContentPanningGesture` so the scroll container owns vertical gestures, but the rule is **platform + content-type specific**:

| Content type | Detection | iOS | Android |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Scrollable `Content` (`scrollable={true}`) | `isScrollable` | Content panning **disabled** (scroll view owns gestures) | Content panning **left enabled** — disabling it makes the backdrop's press-to-close win inner taps (PAH-430) |
| Virtualized list (`List` / `SectionList` / `FlashList`) | `isVirtualizedList` | Default (enabled) | Content panning **disabled** — otherwise the sheet's content-pan gesture captures swipes before `BottomSheetFlatList` and the list cannot scroll |
| Static `Content` (`BottomSheetView`) | neither | Default (enabled) | Default (enabled) |

In all cases an explicit `enableContentPanningGesture` prop from the consumer wins. Users can still close via the handle or backdrop.

**Why Android virtualized lists are special:** PAH-430 only mandates keeping content panning enabled for **static / scrollable-`Content`** layouts on Android. Virtualized lists are a separate code path (`renderBottomSheetLayout`) with the opposite symptom — leaving content panning enabled blocks list scroll — so they get their own Android rule.

### Sheet not rendering

Ensure you have wrapped your app with the required providers:

```tsx
<GestureHandlerRootView style={{ flex: 1 }}>
  <BottomSheetModalProvider>
    <YourApp />
  </BottomSheetModalProvider>
</GestureHandlerRootView>
```

### Dynamic sizing not working with lists

Virtualized lists (List, SectionList, FlashList) require fixed `snapPoints` because their content height is not known upfront. **The component automatically disables dynamic sizing when virtualized lists are detected** and logs a warning in development mode.

```tsx
// WORKS but logs warning - dynamic sizing auto-disabled
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef}>
  <EtBottomSheet.List data={items} ... />
</EtBottomSheet>

// RECOMMENDED - explicitly provide snapPoints
<EtBottomSheet bottomSheetRef={sheetRef} snapPoints={['50%', '90%']}>
  <EtBottomSheet.List data={items} ... />
</EtBottomSheet>
```

### Gesture conflicts with custom components

Wrap components that have their own gesture handling with `NativeViewGestureHandler`:

```tsx
import { NativeViewGestureHandler } from 'react-native-gesture-handler';

<NativeViewGestureHandler disallowInterruption={true}>
  <YourGestureComponent />
</NativeViewGestureHandler>;
```

### Nested/Stacked Bottom Sheets

When presenting multiple sheets, use the library's default stack behavior. Sheets presented via `present()` will automatically stack on top of each other. The `BottomSheetModalProvider` manages the stack order.

## Accessibility

The component provides comprehensive accessibility support:

### Screen Reader Announcements

The sheet automatically announces state changes to screen readers:

- **On open**: Announces `"{sheetName} opened"` when the sheet becomes visible
- **On close**: Announces `"{sheetName} closed"` after the dismiss animation completes

The `sheetName` is derived from (in priority order):

1. `accessibilityLabel` prop
2. Title text from `EtBottomSheet.Header.Title` (auto-extracted)
3. Fallback: "Bottom sheet"

The "opened" announcement is delayed to ensure the sheet is visually present. Delay is preset-specific (`smooth`: 350ms, `bouncy`: 450ms, `fast`: 250ms) and instant when reduced motion is enabled. If preset spring configs change, update `ACCESSIBILITY_ANNOUNCEMENT_DELAYS` in `utils/et-bottom-sheet.const.ts`.

### Modal Behavior

The sheet uses `accessibilityViewIsModal={true}`, which:

- Focuses screen reader on sheet content
- Prevents interaction with content behind the sheet
- Follows iOS VoiceOver and Android TalkBack best practices

### Reduced Motion Support

The component respects the user's reduced motion preference:

- Uses `useReducedMotion` hook to detect system preference
- Applies `REDUCED_MOTION_SPRING_CONFIG` regardless of `animationPreset` (faster, no bounce)
- Maintains functionality while reducing visual motion

### Animation Presets

`animationPreset` controls spring physics for open, close, and snap transitions (distinct from `enableOverDrag`, which only affects manual drag past snap points):

| Preset | Feel | `overshootClamping` |
|--------|------|---------------------|
| `bouncy` (default) | Slight overshoot on settle — v1 default | `false` |
| `smooth` | Subtle spring, minimal bounce | `false` |
| `fast` | Snappy, overdamped | `true` |

Reduced motion overrides all presets.

### Touch Targets

All interactive elements use `Header.Action` which provides:

- Minimum touch targets with proper hit slop configuration
- `accessibilityRole="button"` by default
- `accessibilityLabel` support

## Design Decisions

### No built-in haptic feedback

The old `SimpleHeader` included `expo-haptics` (`Haptics.impactAsync(ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light)`) on close button press. This was intentionally removed during the compound header refactor. `Header.Action` is a generic pressable primitive — haptic feedback is a UX-level concern that belongs in the consumer's `onPress` handler, not baked into the component. Consumers that want haptics can add them explicitly:

```tsx
<EtBottomSheet.Header.Action
  onPress={() => {
    Haptics.impactAsync(Haptics.ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light);
    sheetRef.current?.dismiss();
  }}
  accessibilityLabel="Close"
>
```

## Development Notes

### Internal Architecture

The component uses utility functions for child processing:

**`parseBottomSheetChildren`** - A pure utility function that separates children into header, content, and footer sections:

- Validates that only one of each subcomponent type is present
- Extracts metadata like `isScrollable` and `headerTitle` for accessibility
- `headerTitle` is extracted by inspecting Header's children for a `Header.Title` subcomponent
- **Error handling:**
  - Uses `console.error` (not throw) to match React patterns - allows partial rendering
  - In development: Also logs stack trace via `console.trace` for easier debugging
  - Warns if sheet has no content at all (dev only)

**`renderBottomSheetLayout`** - A render helper function (returns JSX but contains no hooks or state) that renders the appropriate layout structure based on content type:

- **Virtualized list**: Header fixed, list handles scrolling, padding via `contentContainerStyle`
- **Scrollable content**: Header fixed, `BottomSheetScrollView` for content, padding spacer as View
- **Static content**: `BottomSheetView` for dynamic sizing, all content inline

**Bottom padding behavior** (all layout modes):

- With footer: Uses footer height as padding to prevent content from being hidden
- Without footer: Uses `max(20px, bottomInset)` to ensure content clears the home indicator

### Context Architecture

The component uses a **split context pattern** for performance optimization:

**`BottomSheetConfigContext`** - Static configuration (rarely changes):

- `showHandle`, `closeOnBackdrop`, `enablePanDownToClose`
- Theme colors (extracted subset, not entire colors object)
- Components consuming only config won't re-render on state changes

**`BottomSheetStateContext`** - Dynamic state (changes on interaction):

- `isPresented`, `isLoading`
- `dismiss()`, `handleClose()` callbacks
- Components consuming state will re-render when presentation changes

### Constants Architecture

Constants are **co-located with their components** for better maintainability:

**Shared constants** (`utils/et-bottom-sheet.const.ts`):

- Animation configs (`BOUNCY_SPRING_CONFIG`, `SMOOTH_SPRING_CONFIG`, `FAST_SPRING_CONFIG`, `REDUCED_MOTION_SPRING_CONFIG`)
- Layout (`PADDING_VERTICAL`, `SCROLLABLE_CONTENT_MAX_HEIGHT_RATIO`)

**Component-specific constants** (co-located):

- `header/et-bottom-sheet-header.const.ts`:
  - `HEADER_PADDING_HORIZONTAL` (X6 / 24px)
  - `HEADER_PADDING_VERTICAL` (X3 / 12px)
  - `HEADER_MIN_HEIGHT` (44px — aligned with iOS HIG minimum touch target)

### React 19 & React Compiler

This component is designed for React 19 with React Compiler enabled.

**React 19 patterns used:**

- **Function components only**: No class components or legacy patterns
- **Modern ref handling**: Uses `RefObject<BottomSheetModal | null>` with explicit null (React 19 strict mode compatible)
- **JSX namespace**: Uses `React.JSX.Element` return type
- **No `forwardRef`**: Refs passed via `bottomSheetRef` prop (recommended for imperative APIs in React 19)

**React Compiler optimization:**

This project has React Compiler enabled (`reactCompiler: true` in app.json).

- Manual `useMemo`, `useCallback`, and `React.memo` calls have been **removed** from this component
- The compiler automatically adds memoization where beneficial at build time
- No manual memoization is needed - the compiler handles optimization

